4. WHY IT BEATS THE OTHER TWO (one line each):
   - Beats (a) atomic claim+send: atomicity needs a real cross-process atomic
     primitive (bigger design, R3 already accepted the limit); TTL closes the
     permanent-silence failure inside the CURRENT design for ~40 lines.
   - Beats (b) traceability grind: traceability is measured, ratcheted, and
     rising (24.0% -> 30.6%) with zero user impact per point; a stranded claim
     is a household silently never told about a price hike, i.e. the feature
     failing at its one job.

5. HOW IT WOULD BE VERIFIED (paste-and-run commands):
   ```
   cd /home/zoltan/receipts-lens
   python3 -c "
