   s = ProductService(':memory:')
   assert s.claim_price_alert_sent('t','M',100,'2026-10') is True
   # simulate stale claim: backdate notified_at past TTL, re-claim must win
   s._db.execute(\"UPDATE price_alert_sent SET notified_at='2000-01-01T00:00:00'\")
   assert s.claim_price_alert_sent('t','M',100,'2026-10') is True
   print('TTL re-claim works; fresh-claim suppression covered by existing suite')
   "
   pytest tests/test_price_alert_concurrency.py tests/test_price_alert_release_paths.py tests/test_price_alert_f2_5.py -q
   ```
   Pass = re-claim-after-TTL wins, fresh claim still suppresses (existing
   concurrency/release tests stay green), full suite afterwards per method.

6. WHAT IT MUST NOT TOUCH (sprawl guard):
